+### Behavior
+
+Enabled monitoring uses the selected mode and falls back to interaction monitoring when the camera is unavailable. Turning it off suppresses normal-driving monitoring alerts, monitoring-triggered deceleration and lockout; Driver View may still run the camera model for preview.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Find this exception setting through Carrot Web search. The saved choice persists across ignition cycles and restarts; changing it does not change the monitoring mode or web-video setting.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Backup, QR and profiles do not transfer this setting. A normal restore preserves the current device value; resetting defaults restores monitoring. The vehicle CANCEL gesture changes only temporary session state.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
+
