+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+Shadow keeps native-model control while comparing the external result. Active requests still require the exact model/device validation record and the existing stopped, disengaged conditions.
+
+An App session pins the exact model selected offroad. A changed or unloaded App model ends that session; onroad changes are never adopted automatically.
+Compatible hosts receive saved Wi-Fi profiles over the private connection during offroad preparation. Passwords stay out of status files and logs. Verified legacy-model transfer stops on cable loss or onroad transition.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Select the App model while offroad, then use Shadow to compare it. After an active-session loss, stop with controls disengaged, acknowledge through Off or Shadow, and request activation again only with a matching validation record.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Model generation and wire protocol are separate: the source Cinque v2 graph is distinct from the retained native Cinque v3 compatibility option. Readiness and host/ARM tests do not supply device or numerical acceptance.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
+
 <!-- CARROT:MANUAL:END JetlinkMode -->
 
 <!-- CARROT:SETTING:END JetlinkMode -->
